                    Calculation Logic
                </h2>

            </div>

            <h3>
                Higher Is Better
            </h3>

            <div class="formula">
If value >= target:
    Score = 100

If warning <= value < target:
    Score = 75 + ((value - warning) / (target - warning)) × 25

If critical <= value < warning:
    Score = 40 + ((value - critical) / (warning - critical)) × 35

If value < critical:
    Score = (value / critical) × 40
            </div>


            <h3>
                Lower Is Better
            </h3>

            <div class="formula">
If value <= target:
    Score = 100

If target < value <= warning:
    Score = 75 + ((warning - value) / (warning - target)) × 25

If warning < value <= critical:
    Score = 40 + ((critical - value) / (critical - warning)) × 35

If value > critical:
    Score = 0
            </div>


            <h3>
                Automation Coverage
            </h3>

            <div class="formula">
Automation Coverage Score = Actual Automation Percentage

Example:
86% automation → 86 score
75% automation → 75 score
100% automation → 100 score
            </div>


            <h3>
                Missing Data
            </h3>

            <div class="formula">
Missing metric value = 0 score

The metric weight is still included.

Missing category data = 0 score

The category weight is still included.

Example:

Category score = 73
Category weight = 30%

Contribution = 73 × 30%
             = 21.90

Therefore:
Overall Score contribution = 21.90
            </div>

        </section>


